Patch summary:
lavapipe: backport CPU-based ETC2/EAC and ASTC LDR texture emulation.

Backport of Mesa main merge request 38621 (all but its BC commit, as lavapipe
samples BC natively):

- 8ff175f0 util: Move ETC2 decompression to src/util
- f34e4061 lavapipe: Refactor image plane allocation into helper function
- afa87d9c lavapipe: Add CPU-based ASTC/ETC2 texture decompression emulation
- c579a989 lavapipe: Decompress zero-initialized emulated images on layout
  transition

llvmpipe cannot sample ETC2 or ASTC, so lavapipe reported
textureCompressionETC2 and textureCompressionASTC_LDR as off. Chromium's
Graphite renderer (Dawn) requires ETC2 on Android, so with guest_lavapipe
Chromium's GPU process failed ("Requested feature
FeatureName::TextureCompressionETC2 is not supported") and the browser quit
("GPU process isn't usable. Goodbye."); ANGLE also stopped at OpenGL ES 3.1
for want of ASTC. Compressed images now keep a second, uncompressed plane that
uploads and host copies decompress into on the CPU, and that views sample.

The upstream commits apply unchanged (less the CI file); the one addition is
texcompress_etc.c in src/util/Android.bp, which external-mesa3d.patch
generates without it. Drop this patch, and regenerate external-mesa3d.patch,
when the Mesa pin includes the merge request.

